# Caption card

When the user asks for a **caption card**, use this composite layout: a primary white card body plus an optional grey caption strip attached below (one visual unit).

## Structure

```tsx
<div className="rounded-md bg-card shadow-[var(--shadow-card)] overflow-hidden">
  {/* Main content — keep prominent */}
  <div className="p-6">
    {children}
  </div>

  {/* Caption — secondary info only; render when there is content to show */}
  {caption && (
    <div className="border-t border-gray-200 bg-gray-100/90 px-6 py-4 dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800/50">
      <p className="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">{label}</p>
      <p className="text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-heading mt-1">{value}</p>
      {detail && (
        <p className="text-xs text-muted mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">{detail}</p>
      )}
    </div>
  )}
</div>
```

## Rules

- Do **not** use a separate `Card` for the caption — attach it to the parent block.
- Main fields stay in the white `p-6` section; hints, balances, and meta belong in the grey strip.
- Caption typography: label (uppercase muted xs) → value (semibold sm heading) → detail (muted xs).
- Use `tabular-nums` on numeric values.
- Do not use loud borders, accent fills, or `AvailableQtyHint` for caption-card content.
- Reference: seller remaining balance on PO entry (`OrderEntryPage` → Seller & Item block).
